Andy Clarke [demonstrates one of the hottest CSS3 features](http://blog.typekit.com/2011/01/25/case-study-getting-hardboiled-with-css3-2d-transforms/): using `transform` to manipulate the size, placement and even *rotation* of elements. (And, as if that weren’t enough, tosses in some cool `:nth-of-type` pseudo selector action, eliminating the need for unnecessary `id` or `class` attributes in your markup.)
